                                                    titleEn: "Bi-transitive & Dual-Voice Verbs: 1) Dvikarmak (Contains 2 objects): Direct Object (Pratyaksha: inanimate thing, in Prathama/Dvitiya) and Indirect Object (Apratyaksha: animate recipient, in Chaturthi); e.g., 'Grandmother told a story to grandson' (Grandson = Indirect, Story = Direct); 2) Ubhayavidha Verbs: Same verb operating both transitively and intransitively (e.g., 'He opened the door' vs 'The door opened')",
