                                                    titleEn: "Compound, Causative, Potential & Impersonal Verbs: 1) Compound Verb (Sanyukta = Verbal Participle Dhatusadhit + Auxiliary Sahayyak; e.g., Khelu laagla); 2) Causative (Prayojak: Subject causes external object to act; e.g., Mother makes child laugh - Hasvite); 3) Potential (Shakya: Inherent capacity; e.g., Chalvate, Chadhvato); 4) Impersonal/Bhavakartruk: Subject is unexpressed, embedded within verbal mood itself (e.g., Ujaadale, Gadgadle, Sanjaavle)",
