                                                    titleEn: "Three Structural Sentence Types: 1) Keval Vakya (Simple: Single independent clause with one subject and one finite predicate); 2) Mishra Vakya (Complex: One dominant principal clause linked to one or more subordinate dependent clauses via subordinating conjunctions; e.g., 'When rain falls, farmers sow'); 3) Sanyukta Vakya (Compound: Two independent coordinate clauses conjoined via coordinating conjunctions; e.g., 'Lightning struck AND rain began')",
