                                                    titleMr: "कारकाचे नियम (Nominative vs Objective Case): १) 'Than' किंवा 'As' नंतर तुलना दोन कर्त्यांमध्ये होत असल्यास Nominative (Subjective) Case वापरावी: उदा. 'He is taller than I' ('than me' बोलचालीत चालते पण व्याकरणदृष्ट्या 'I' बरोबर आहे); २) 'Let', 'Between', 'Except', 'But' आणि कोणत्याही Preposition नंतर नेहमी Objective Case वापरावी: उदा. 'Let him and me go' (Let he and I चुकीचे); 'There is no dispute between you and me' (between you and I चुकीचे आहे); ३) 'Each other' (दोघांसाठी) vs 'One another' (दोघांपेक्षा जास्त व्यक्तींसाठी)",
                                                    titleEn: "Case Governance Principles: 1) Nominative case follows 'Than' or 'As' when comparing subjects ('He runs faster than I [do]', NOT 'me'); 2) Objective case strictly follows 'Let', 'Between', 'Except', 'But', and all prepositions ('Between you and me', NOT 'between you and I'; 'Let him and her work'); 3) Reciprocal pronouns: 'Each other' for two entities, 'One another' for three or more entities",
                                                    chips: ["He is taller than I (than me चुकीचे)", "Between you and me (preposition नंतर objective)", "Let him and me go", "Each other (२ जण) vs One another (३+ जण)"]
