                                                    titleEn: "Relative Pronouns ('Who', 'Whom', 'That'): 'Who' functions as subjective operator (substitutes He/She); 'Whom' functions as objective operator (substitutes Him/Her); Restrictive Relative Pronoun 'That' is MANDATORY after: All, Same, Only, None, Any, Nothing, and Superlative Adjectives ('All that glitters is not gold'; 'Man is the only animal that can talk')",
