                                                    titleMr: "कथनाचे मूलभूत नियम व काळातील बदल (Tense Backshifting): Reporting Verb भूतकाळात (Said / Said to) असल्यास Inverted Commas मधील काळाचा भूतकाळ होतो; १) Simple Present $\to$ Simple Past; २) Present Continuous $\to$ Past Continuous; ३) Present Perfect $\to$ Past Perfect; ४) Simple Past (V2) $\to$ Past Perfect (Had + V3); ५) Modals: Will $\to$ Would, Shall $\to$ Should/Would, Can $\to$ Could, May $\to$ Might; शब्दांमधील बदल: Now $\to$ Then, Here $\to$ There, This $\to$ That, Today $\to$ That day, Yesterday $\to$ The previous day / The day before, Tomorrow $\to$ The next day",
                                                    titleEn: "Tense Backshifting & Deictic Temporal Shifts: When Reporting Verb is in Past tense (said/said to), the reported clause shifts backward: Simple Present $\to$ Simple Past; Present Continuous $\to$ Past Continuous; Simple Past $\to$ Past Perfect; Present Perfect $\to$ Past Perfect; Modals shift (Will $\to$ Would, Can $\to$ Could, May $\to$ Might); Deictic shifts: Today $\to$ That day, Yesterday $\to$ The previous day, Tomorrow $\to$ The next day, Now $\to$ Then",
