                                                    titleEn: "Adverbial Positioning & 'Enough' Syntax: Adverbs qualify verbs, adjectives, or other adverbs; 1) Rule of 'Enough': When modifying an adjective or adverb, 'enough' is placed POST-POSITIVELY immediately AFTER the modified word ('He is wise enough', NOT 'enough wise'; 'Ran fast enough'); 2) 'Too' conveys excessive negative consequence ('too weak to walk'); 3) Invariant forms: 'Fast', 'Hard', 'Late' operate as both adjectives and adverbs ('Fastly' is an illegitimate pseudo-word)",
