                                                    titleEn: "Modal Possibility Heuristics: 1) If no negative boundary or explicit restriction exists between two disjoint sets, all possibilities between them are logically VALID; 2) What is already a 100% established fact CANNOT be considered a possibility (Definite True + Possibility = FALSE); 3) 'Can never be' represents a definite negative deduction, NOT a modal possibility",
