                                                    titleEn: "Three Canonical Remainder Paradigms: Case 1 (Constant remainder $r$): Smallest number $= \text{LCM}(x,y,z) + r$; Case 2 (Variable remainder with uniform difference $d = x-a = y-b = z-c$): Smallest number $= \text{LCM}(x,y,z) - d$; Case 3 (Largest divisor leaving identical unknown remainder $r$ when dividing $x,y,z$): Divisor $= \text{HCF}(|x-y|, |y-z|, |z-x|)$",
                                                    chips: ["समान बाकी सूत्र $= \\text{LCM} + r$", "फरक समान सूत्र $= \\text{LCM} - d$", "मोठ्यात मोठी संख्या $= \\text{HCF}(|x-y|, |y-z|)$"]
