                                                    titleEn: "Quarterly Compounding & Variable Annual Rates: 1) Compounded Quarterly: 4 compounding periods annually; Divide nominal rate by 4 ($R/4$) and multiply time by 4 ($4N$): $A = P \left(1 + \frac{R}{400}\right)^{4N}$; 2) Successive Variable Rates: If rates are $R_1\%, R_2\%, R_3\%$ across consecutive years: $A = P \left(1 + \frac{R_1}{100}\right)\left(1 + \frac{R_2}{100}\right)\left(1 + \frac{R_3}{100}\right)$",
