                                                titleEn: "Gubernatorial Discretion (Articles 163 & 200): Unlike the President who lacks explicit constitutional discretion, Article 163 specifically vests the Governor with constitutional discretion; Governor's discretionary decisions cannot be questioned; 1) Article 200: Discretion to reserve state bills for President's consideration (mandatory if bill imperils High Court powers); 2) Article 356: Discretion to report breakdown of constitutional machinery; 3) Discretion in hung assemblies and floor-test directives; Shamsher Singh (1974) and Nabam Rebia (2016) benchmarks held discretion cannot be arbitrary or capricious",
