                                                titleEn: "Parliamentary Privileges (Art 105) & Joint Sittings (Art 108): 1) Privileges under Art 105: Absolute freedom of speech within chambers (exempt from judicial proceedings); Immunity from arrest in civil cases 40 days before, during, and 40 days after sessions (no civil immunity for criminal arrest); 2) Joint Sitting (Article 108): Summoned by President to resolve legislative deadlocks on Ordinary Bills pending >6 months; Presided by Speaker of Lok Sabha; Decided by simple majority of total members present and voting; Prohibited for Money Bills and Constitution Amendment Bills",
