                                                titleEn: "Comptroller & Auditor General of India (Articles 148-151): 1) Article 148: Described by Dr. Ambedkar as the 'most important officer under the Constitution'; 'Guardian of the Public Purse'; Appointed by President; Tenure: 6 years or 65 years of age; Removable on identical grounds as Supreme Court judge via parliamentary address; Ineligible for further government office post-retirement; 2) Independence: Salary charged on Consolidated Fund of India (cannot be varied to disadvantage); 3) Article 149: Audits all receipts and expenditures of Union, States, and public sector undertakings; 4) Article 151: Submits 3 audit reports to President: Appropriation Accounts, Finance Accounts, and Public Undertakings, which are laid before Parliament",
