                                                titleEn: "Legislative Power Imbalance & Dilatory Limits: Unlike Rajya Sabha, the Legislative Council is remarkably weak; 1) Ordinary Bills: If rejected or stalled by Council, Assembly can pass it a second time; Council can delay an ordinary bill for maximum 3 months in 1st round and maximum 1 month in 2nd round (MAXIMUM DELAY OF 4 MONTHS); Thereafter, bill is deemed passed in the form approved by Assembly; State legislatures have ZERO PROVISION FOR JOINT SITTINGS; 2) Money Bills: Council can delay strictly for 14 days; 3) Nagpur Pact 1953: Mandates holding at least one annual session (Winter Session) at Nagpur",
                                                chips: ["विधानपरिषद कमाल ४ महिने विलंब करू शकते (३ + १ महिना)", "राज्य विधिमंडळात संयुक्त बैठक नसते (No Joint Sitting)", "धन विधेयक १४ दिवस", "नागपूर हिवाळी अधिवेशन (नागपूर करार १९५३)"]
