                                                titleEn: "Bombay High Court & Public Interest Litigation (PIL): 1) Bombay High Court: Established 14 August 1862 under High Courts Act 1861; Territorial jurisdiction over Maharashtra, Goa, and Dadra & Nagar Haveli and Daman & Diu; Principal seat at Mumbai with 3 Permanent Benches at Nagpur, Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar, and Panaji; Retirement age 62; 2) Public Interest Litigation (PIL): Pioneered in 1980s by Justice P.N. Bhagwati and Justice V.R. Krishna Iyer; Relaxed the traditional doctrine of 'Locus Standi' allowing any public-spirited citizen or group to move the court for protection of public interest",
