                                                    titleEn: "Primary Soil Classes & Chemistry: 1) Black Regur Soil: Formed via basalt weathering; Covers 75-80% of state; Black hue caused by Titaniferous Magnetite; High clay content with exceptional moisture retention; Rich in lime/potash, deficient in nitrogen/phosphorus; Ideal for cotton, sugarcane, jowar; 2) Laterite Soil: South Konkan (Ratnagiri, Sindhudurg) and Mahabaleshwar; Developed via intense leaching (silica leached away leaving iron and aluminium sesquioxides); Acidic; Famed for Alphonso mango, cashew, betel nut; 3) Red-Yellow Soil: Derived from ancient Archaean rocks in East Vidarbha; High iron content; Ideal for paddy",
