                                                    titleEn: "Western Ghats Biodiversity Hotspot & Conservation Committees: 1) Western Ghats: Designated among world's 36 hyper-diverse Biodiversity Hotspots (Norman Myers); UNESCO inscribed 39 sites as World Natural Heritage in 2012 (includes Kaas Plateau Flower Valley, Chandoli, Koyna, Radhanagari); 2) Madhav Gadgil Committee (WGEEP 2011): Recommended grading entire Western Ghats into 3 Ecologically Sensitive Zones (ESZ) with ban on mining/dams; 3) K. Kasturirangan Panel (2013): Scaled down ESA protection strictly to 37% natural landscape area",
