                                                    titleEn: "Bretton Woods Institutional Twins (IMF & World Bank): Born from 1944 conference; HQ Washington D.C.; 1) International Monetary Fund (IMF): Stabilizes international monetary system and provides short-to-medium term liquidity for Balance of Payments crises; Unit of Account: Special Drawing Rights (SDR 'Paper Gold') based on 5-currency basket (USD, EUR, CNY, JPY, GBP); 2) World Bank Group: Extends long-term developmental project loans; Comprises 5 affiliates: a) IBRD, b) IDA ('Soft Loan Window' extending interest-free zero-coupon credits to poorest nations), c) IFC (private sector equity/debt), d) MIGA, e) ICSID (Investment disputes tribunal - India is NOT a member)",
