                                                    titleEn: "New Industrial Policy 1991 & Disinvestment Policy: 1) Industrial Policy Statement (24 July 1991 under Rao-Manmohan duo): Abolished license-permit raj across manufacturing sectors (retained mandatory licensing only for alcohol, tobacco, hazardous chemicals, industrial explosives); Public sector reservation slashed from 17 down strictly to 2 strategic domains: a) Atomic Energy, b) Railway Operations; 2) Disinvestment: Liquidating equity in Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) overseen by DIPAM under Ministry of Finance; Strategic disinvestment vs Minority stake sales; 3) Production Linked Incentive (PLI Scheme): Direct fiscal cash incentives of 4-6% on incremental sales to boost domestic manufacturing scale",
