                                                    titleEn: "Cyber Attack Vectors, IT Act 2000 & CERT-In: 1) Threat Paradigms: Malware; Ransomware (encrypts data files demanding cryptocurrency ransom; e.g., WannaCry); Phishing (social engineering identity theft); Spyware (covert surveillance implants; e.g., Pegasus); 2) Information Technology Act 2000: Enacted to legalize e-commerce and penalize cybercrimes; Section 66 penalizes hacking; Section 66A Struck Down: SC in historic Shreya Singhal v. Union of India (2015) invalidated Section 66A as unconstitutional violation of Article 19(1)(a) freedom of speech; 3) CERT-In: National nodal agency under MeitY operational since 2004 responding to cybersecurity incidents",
