                                                    titleEn: "Recombinant DNA & Animal Cloning: 1) Recombinant DNA (rDNA) Technology: Constructing chimeric DNA combining fragments from diverse genomes; Essential Tools: Restriction Endonucleases ('Molecular Scissors' cleaving DNA at specific palindromic recognition sequences), DNA Ligase ('Molecular Glue' sealing phosphodiester backbones), Vectors/Plasmids; Enabled synthesis of recombinant human insulin (Humulin); 2) Cloning: Asexual genesis of genetically identical organisms via Somatic Cell Nuclear Transfer (SCNT); Ian Wilmut cloned 'Dolly the Sheep' on 5 July 1996 at Roslin Institute, Scotland (first mammal cloned from adult somatic cell)",
