                                                    titleEn: "CRISPR-Cas9 Gene Editing & DNA Fingerprinting: 1) CRISPR-Cas9: Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeats; Targeted molecular genomic editing; Emmanuelle Charpentier & Jennifer Doudna won 2020 Nobel Prize in Chemistry; Guide RNA directs Cas9 endonuclease to precise genomic addresses to excise defective mutations, treating genetic disorders like Sickle Cell Anemia; 2) DNA Fingerprinting: Invented by Alec Jeffreys (1984); Pioneered in India by Dr. Lalji Singh at CCMB Hyderabad; Analyzes polymorphic Variable Number Tandem Repeats (VNTRs) for forensic criminal conviction and disputed paternity verification",
