                                                    titleEn: "Nanoscale Physics & Quantum Manifestations: 1) Nanoscale Metrics: 1 nanometer ($1\text{ nm}$) $= 10^{-9}$ meters; Defined as engineering matter at 1 to 100 nm scale; 2) Quantum Mechanical Shifts: At nanoscale, the Surface Area to Volume Ratio surges astronomically, radically enhancing chemical reactivity, mechanical tensile strength, and optical/electrical conductivity; 3) Genesis: Conceptualized by Richard Feynman in 1959 landmark lecture ('There's Plenty of Room at the Bottom'); Term 'Nanotechnology' coined by Norio Taniguchi in 1974",
