                                                    titleEn: "Nanomaterials, Agronomic Nano-Urea & Oncology: 1) Carbon Nanotubes (CNTs): Cylindrical carbon allotrope hollow tubes; 100 times stronger than structural steel at one-sixth the weight; Superior ballistic thermal/electrical conductors; 2) Graphene: 2D monolayer honeycomb lattice of $sp^2$ carbon; Andre Geim & Konstantin Novoselov won 2010 Nobel in Physics; Thinnest, strongest material known; 3) Nano-Urea Liquid: Developed by IFFCO at Kalol (Gujarat); 500 ml bottle replaces an entire 45-kg bag of conventional granular urea; Yields >80% nitrogen absorption efficiency via foliar spraying, reducing groundwater leaching; 4) Targeted Nanomedicine: Gold nanoparticles directly delivering cytotoxic chemotherapy to oncology tumors sparing healthy cells",
